  "question": {
    "text": "Phenol treated with chloroform in presence of sodium hydroxide, which further hydrolysed in presence of an acid results"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Salicyclic acid",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Benzene-1,2-diol",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Benzene-1, 3-diol",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2-Hydroxybenzaldehyde",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Chloroform <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></math> in the presence of an alkali <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>NaOH</mi></mfenced></math> undergoes formylation of phenol at the ortho-position. This is also called as the Reimer-Tiemann reaction.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0031_8df290d7835a.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 164px;\"/>Hence, the answer is option D.</p>"
  }
